From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipmr: do not drop GSO packets that fit the MTU after
 segmentation

ipmr_prepare_xmit() drops any packet with DF set whose length (plus
encapsulation) exceeds the egress MTU, without accounting for GSO.  A
GSO packet that will be segmented on xmit into pieces that each fit the
MTU is therefore dropped even though it is perfectly sendable.

Validate the packet against the MTU with skb_gso_validate_network_len()
instead, so that only packets whose resulting segments would exceed the
MTU are dropped.

Fixes: 9fd1ff5d2ac7 ("udp: Support UDP fraglist GRO/GSO.")
---
 net/ipv4/ipmr.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/ipv4/ipmr.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/ipmr.c
@@ -1891,6 +1891,7 @@ static int ipmr_prepare_xmit(struct net *net, struct mr_table *mrt,
 	struct rtable *rt;
 	struct flowi4 fl4;
 	int    encap = 0;
+	unsigned int mtu;
 
 	vif_dev = vif_dev_read(vif);
 	if (!vif_dev)
@@ -1923,7 +1924,9 @@ static int ipmr_prepare_xmit(struct net *net, struct mr_table *mrt,
 			return -1;
 	}
 
-	if (skb->len+encap > dst4_mtu(&rt->dst) && (ntohs(iph->frag_off) & IP_DF)) {
+	mtu = dst4_mtu(&rt->dst) - encap;
+	if (skb->len > mtu && (ntohs(iph->frag_off) & IP_DF) &&
+	    !(skb_is_gso(skb) && skb_gso_validate_network_len(skb, mtu))) {
 		/* Do not fragment multicasts. Alas, IPv4 does not
 		 * allow to send ICMP, so that packets will disappear
 		 * to blackhole.
